# Windows NTFS is case-insensitive, so `.claude/skills/` and `.claude/Skills/` are ONE
# directory here — but git is case-sensitive and would happily commit both spellings.
# On a Linux/macOS checkout that becomes two real directories which then drift apart.
# Track the lowercase spelling only.
.claude/Skills/
